3{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}-30{x}^{2}+36x+12.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(1)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(1)<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=1$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=1$" 13194139535360 true] [17592186345764 1113 #uuid "d1f3f815-5705-5ffe-8f6e-280bb7f8ac8b" 13194139535360 true] [17592186345764 1145 "We're given that $x=1$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}-30{x}^{2}+36x+12,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=12{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}-60x+36.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=36{x}^{2}+24x-60.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1) & =36(1)^{2}+24(1)-60=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is zero, we conclude that the test is inconclusive, we need to use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's  find other stationary points. Solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}-60x+36 & =0 \\\\ 12({x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-5x+3) & =0 \\\\ 12(x-1)({x}^{2}+2x-3) & =0 \\\\ 12(x-1)(x-1)(x+3) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have two stationary points, $x=-3$ and $x=1.$ Next, to determine whether these points are local maxima or minima, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=-4,0,2$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-4) & =12(-4-1)^{2}(-4+3)=-300<0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(0) & =12(0-1)^{2}(0+3)=36>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =12(2-1)^{2}(2+3)=60>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,-3)$ | $-3$ | $(-3,1)$ | $1$ | $(1,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $-4$ |  | $0$ |  | $2$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $-$ | $0$ | $+$ | $0$ | $+$ |\n| $f$ | $↘$ | min | $↗$ |  | $↗$ |\n\nAt $x=1,$  the first derivative does not change the sign. Therefore, $x=1$ is neither a local minimum nor a local maximum.\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\"" 13194139535360 true] [17592186345765 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345766 13194139535360 true] [17592186345765 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345767 13194139535360 true] [17592186345765 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345768 13194139535360 true] [17592186345765 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345769 13194139535360 true] [17592186345765 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345770 13194139535360 true] [17592186345765 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535360 true] [17592186345765 1041 "selection" 13194139535360 true] [17592186345765 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345769 13194139535360 true] [17592186345765 1110 #uuid "48b03e45-4e65-5aa0-a4a6-c1500340df7a" 13194139535360 true] [17592186345766 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535360 true] [17592186345766 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535360 true] [17592186345766 1111 #uuid "a2f9fb7d-1b47-56ca-9dc4-21f64726f4e1" 13194139535360 true] [17592186345767 1034 "III only" 13194139535360 true] [17592186345767 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535360 true] [17592186345767 1111 #uuid "db81d32c-97fd-5a6f-90d6-0cec9d1c1a75" 13194139535360 true] [17592186345768 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535360 true] [17592186345768 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535360 true] [17592186345768 1111 #uuid "ba4f430f-a020-5a09-90b9-3042fd43018c" 13194139535360 true] [17592186345769 1034 "None of the statements are true." 13194139535360 true] [17592186345769 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535360 true] [17592186345769 1111 #uuid "33d84df6-752c-5b1e-bf98-6c7d80b66dc2" 13194139535360 true] [17592186345770 1034 "II only" 13194139535360 true] [17592186345770 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535360 true] [17592186345770 1111 #uuid "1c74a4ee-dc9e-5f77-8ecb-9f24edddc9bd" 13194139535360 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-22011" 17592186345757 "q-22011/selection" 17592186345758 "q-22011/selection/03b99debc8e9534f2364927a2cf1eba83bddd906503dea5d13395ce906a45ab9" 17592186345759 "q-22011/selection/431472f1dab61ef